THIRD-PARTY MODELS AND DATA BUNDLED IN THIS REPOSITORY

The MIT terms above cover the source code. Some files in this repository are
not source code and carry their own terms, which travel with them. Full detail
is in Docs/ATTRIBUTIONS.md and Fixtures/MANIFEST.md.

  Models/esm2_t6_8M_UR50D.mlpackage
  Models/esm2_t6_8M_UR50D.tokeniser.json
  Models/esm2_t6_8M_UR50D.reference.npz
      A Core ML conversion of ESM-2 (facebook/esm2_t6_8M_UR50D), which is
      MIT licensed. Copyright (c) Meta Platforms, Inc. and affiliates.
      Lin et al., "Evolutionary-scale prediction of atomic-level protein
      structure with a language model", Science 379 (2023).

  Models/torsion_tables.json
  Models/flexibility_centroids.json
  Fixtures/structures/AF-*.pdb, AF-*.cif
  Fixtures/api/afdb_*.json, uniprot_*.json
      Derived from, or copied from, the AlphaFold Protein Structure Database
      and UniProtKB, both CC BY 4.0. Copyright EMBL-EBI, and DeepMind
      Technologies Limited for the predictions. CC BY 4.0 permits derivative
      works under any licence provided attribution is preserved, which is why
      the attribution above and in Docs/ATTRIBUTIONS.md must travel with these
      files.

  Fixtures/structures/1bab.pdb, 1bab.cif
      PDB entry 1BAB, from PDBe. Structure data in the PDB archive is CC0.

The conversion pipeline in Tools/coreml uses fair-esm (MIT), PyTorch
(BSD-3-Clause), coremltools (BSD-3-Clause) and NumPy (BSD-3-Clause). None of
these is redistributed here; they are dependencies of the build-time scripts
only, pinned in Tools/coreml/requirements.txt.

No third-party Swift package is used or vendored. The app links Apple system
frameworks (SwiftUI, SceneKit, Core ML, AVFoundation, Swift Charts) under the
terms of the Apple SDK licence.
